                <pb facs="0432" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg420"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.199/43: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                        France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-14T18:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–352. Your 380, October 13, 3 p.m. In view of circumstances reported no further
                    effort should be made for Chapman to visit Spanish territory to investigate
                    Zabala case.</p>
                <p>We are awaiting report from Consul at Seville before taking further action with
                    regard to reopening of Consulate at Bilbao. In the meantime no further action
                    should be taken by you in this regard.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
